# Chaos: HD minimap, the explored map drawn from small pictures of the real items (O543; client/BASE.md "0197"; src/client/chaosminimaphd.h (new, pure),
# minimap.h/.cpp, uiminimap.h/.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, mods/client_settings dataset.lua and options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0196).
# Owner decision 2026-11-13: style "HD painted": real sprites in miniature plus shadows, living water and lava, smooth zoom; HD from 2 px per tile up,
# flat colours below.
#  * Recipe: MinimapTile grows from 3 to 11 bytes. Besides flags, colour and speed it keeps the client ids of the tile's ground, ground border, top
#    decoration and top solid (Minimap::updateTile, chaosRecipe: only items that belong to the map; creatures and things a player drops are left out).
#    .otmm version 2 stores the 11 byte tile. A version 1 file still loads: its blocks are expanded with an empty recipe (chaos::minimaphd::expandV1Block),
#    so an old explored map shows the flat colour squares of before. #pragma pack now ends with the tile (the block holds 64 bit counters).
#  * Swatches: client/tools/gen_minimap_swatches.py makes data/minimap_hd/swatches.png (8 px per tile cell of every item type the map uses, area averaged,
#    alpha weighted, lightly sharpened) and index.txt. g_minimap.loadHdAtlas(dir) reads both; an id without a swatch, a tile without a recipe or an atlas that
#    did not load gives the flat colour square. Nothing leaves the explored area: only tiles the client has seen are drawn.
#  * Compose (chaosminimaphd.h composeBlock): a 64 x 64 block becomes one RGBA picture of 8 px per tile (flat square, ground, border, decoration, then the
#    solid with an alpha boost of 1.55 so a thin wall or tree keeps its body; a 2 x 2 item of the next block spills up and left across the edge, so a ring of 2
#    tiles of the neighbour blocks is read), then the C pass: a shadow south east of walls, rock and trees (light from the north west), a soft contact shadow,
#    a lighter north west rim and a darker south east edge on the tall tiles, a thin dark line where rock meets open ground, water and lava tint, a glow round
#    lava, a little more colour. Then reduced to the texel density of the zoom (2, 4 or 8 px per tile, chaos::minimaphd::lodFor): the engine's texture has no
#    hardware mipmaps, so the picture is made at the size it is drawn. About 6 ms for a block with trees and water (-O2, header benchmark).
#  * Draw: HD blocks go through DrawQueueItemImageWithShader with the shader chaos_minimap_hd (overlay data/shaders, vertex stage chaos_minimap_vertex), which moves
#    water and lava: the picture tells the liquids by its alpha (255 plain, 245 water, 235 lava, 0 not explored), the shader writes alpha 1 back. A block is
#    composed at most once per draw call and a changed block at most every 250 ms (the older picture is drawn meanwhile), so a step that brings new tiles does not
#    stall a frame. Blocks held as HD pictures: an LRU of at least 24 (and twice the blocks in view), evictOldest; the flat 64 x 64 picture of every block stays
#    and is the fallback. Filter: linear (smooth).
#  * Smooth scroll: Minimap::draw, getTilePoint, getTilePosition and getTileRect take the camera's sub tile offset in tiles. UIMinimap::getSubTile follows the
#    local player's walk offset while the camera is on the player's tile (walk offset over the sprite size), so the map glides through a step instead of jumping
#    a tile; HD blocks take the exact shift, flat blocks the shift rounded to a pixel. UIMinimap:setFollowWalk(bool) (default on). One block more at the top and
#    left is walked since the shift can bring it into view. The Lua pins and dots read getTilePoint, so they follow.
#  * Lua: g_minimap.loadHdAtlas(dir), unloadHdAtlas(), setHdEnabled(bool), isHdEnabled(), setHdMinScale(px per tile), getHdSwatchCount(), getHdBlockCount(),
#    getHdMaxBlocks(); UIMinimap:setFollowWalk(bool), isFollowWalk(), getSubTileX(), getSubTileY() (the camera's sub tile offset in tiles, so the Lua dot of the player stays at the camera).
#  * Options (Options > Graphics, under HD monsters): "HD minimap" (dataset `hdMinimap`, default on, no restart; overlay module game_minimaphd) and "Monsters on the
#    minimap" (dataset `minimapRadar`, default on; overlay module game_minimapdots, server radar.lua).
# Checked: applies after 0001-0196 on the base client tree (no fuzz); minimap.cpp, uiminimap.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, map.cpp and client.cpp pass
# g++ -std=c++20 -fsyntax-only; the header passes client/tools/chaosminimaphd_test.cpp (also with -fsanitize=address,undefined); the shaders pass glslangValidator
# (desktop 1.10 and ES 1.00). Not built, linked or run in a client.
